Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• “collection_name”: restrict the search to the TCGA‑BRCA collection.  
• “Modality”: select whole‑slide microscopy objects (value = ‘SM’).  
• “SpecimenPreparationSequence”: VARIANT column that stores the nested JSON describing all tissue‑preparation / staining steps; we have to look for an eosin‑related step inside this JSON.  
• “NumberOfFrames”: contains the number of frames (tiles) in each WSI object; summing it across the selected objects gives the requested total frame count.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1.  Check which imaging modalities exist in TCGA‑BRCA
SELECT DISTINCT "Modality"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE  "collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  List a few SM objects from TCGA‑BRCA with their frame counts
SELECT "SOPInstanceUID",
       "NumberOfFrames",
       "SeriesInstanceUID"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE  "collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  "Modality"        = 'SM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Preview the full JSON stored in SpecimenPreparationSequence for an SM instance
SELECT "SOPInstanceUID",
       "SpecimenPreparationSequence"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE  "collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  "Modality"        = 'SM'
  AND  "SpecimenPreparationSequence" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4.  Flatten level‑1 of SpecimenPreparationSequence for a single SM instance
SELECT t."SOPInstanceUID",
       f.value AS "prep_step_json"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN (INPUT => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE  t."collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  t."Modality"        = 'SM'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5.  Look for any preparation steps whose JSON (level‑1) text contains ‘eosin’
SELECT DISTINCT t."SOPInstanceUID"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN (INPUT => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE  t."collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  t."Modality"        = 'SM'
  AND  f.value::STRING ILIKE '%eosin%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6.  Verify a few SM instances that satisfy the eosin criterion and view their frame counts
SELECT t."SOPInstanceUID",
       t."NumberOfFrames",
       t."SeriesInstanceUID"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN (INPUT => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE  t."collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  t."Modality"        = 'SM'
  AND  f.value::STRING ILIKE '%eosin%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7.  Aggregate the qualifying instances: count of objects and total frames
SELECT COUNT(*)                            AS "num_wsi_objects",
       SUM(TRY_TO_NUMBER("NumberOfFrames")) AS "total_frames"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN (INPUT => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE  t."collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  t."Modality"        = 'SM'
  AND  f.value::STRING ILIKE '%eosin%';
```

```sql
-- 8.  Same aggregation at series level (if multiple instances per series)
SELECT t."SeriesInstanceUID",
       COUNT(*)                            AS "instances_in_series",
       SUM(TRY_TO_NUMBER("NumberOfFrames")) AS "frames_in_series"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN (INPUT => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE  t."collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  t."Modality"        = 'SM'
  AND  f.value::STRING ILIKE '%eosin%'
GROUP BY t."SeriesInstanceUID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9.  Quick sanity check: list any remaining SM instances whose JSON does NOT mention eosin
SELECT COUNT(*) AS "sm_without_eosin"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL
WHERE  "collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  "Modality"        = 'SM'
  AND  "SpecimenPreparationSequence" IS NOT NULL
  AND  "SOPInstanceUID" NOT IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT t."SOPInstanceUID"
        FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL t,
               LATERAL FLATTEN (INPUT => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
        WHERE  t."collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
          AND  t."Modality"        = 'SM'
          AND  f.value::STRING ILIKE '%eosin%'
      );
```

```sql
-- 10.  Final single‑line answer: total number of frames in all SM WSI with eosin staining
SELECT SUM(TRY_TO_NUMBER("NumberOfFrames")) AS "total_frames_eosin_sm_tcga_brca"
FROM   IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_ALL t,
       LATERAL FLATTEN (INPUT => t."SpecimenPreparationSequence") f
WHERE  t."collection_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND  t."Modality"        = 'SM'
  AND  f.value::STRING ILIKE '%eosin%';
```
